# Review routing: pull requests are authored by the developer identity (the
# account the agent is bound to); review and approval happen as the dedicated
# review account in the browser, and an author cannot self-approve — so the
# wildcard routes every change to the account that actually reviews. The login
# on the routing line is this deployment's fact (paired with lifecycleActor in
# .github/issue-management/config.json). Owners need explicit write access.
